<title>NETHERLANDS: SHARES IN ENDEMOL GAIN ON TV DEAL NEWS.</title>
<headline>SHARES IN ENDEMOL GAIN ON TV DEAL NEWS.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dutch television production company Endemol marched ahead smartly in an otherwise depressed market on Monday, after it announced a three-year deal with German commercial broadcaster RTL Television.</p>
<p>Endemol shares opened up 0.60 guilders at 52.40, adding a further 10 cents to 52.50 in the first half-hour of trade.</p>
<p>This contrasted with a 1.95 percent fall to 1472.48 in the AMX MidCap index, of which it is a component stock.</p>
<p>In April, media reports had suggested the lucrative German contract might be in jeopardy, sending Endemol shares plunging.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
